{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527121-ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5","id":1527121,"title":"Ten Tips to using Touchstones in V5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-20T09:01:34-08:00","id":1527121,"title":"Ten Tips to using Touchstones in V5","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2023/12/ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Touchstones are a controversial but interesting new mechanic to Vampire: The Masquerade Fifth Edition. Previously, it was possible to more or less live your unlife completely separate from the Kine (&quot;cattle&quot;) and move around them with no interactions other than through ghoul henchmen or as food. Touchstones as a tool, however, encourage (some would say &quot;force&quot;) players to have some interaction or care about the mortal world.<br /> <br /> If you want to play a rules accurate player character, there has to be at least one mortal in the world that your Kindred has strong feelings regarding. These feelings do not have to be love or even affection but can include bitter loathing or resentment regarding. A vampire who hates their abusive parent and keeps them locked up in a homemade prison they pay for helps the undead keep in touch with their humanity as perversely as someone that they try to help their nephew get through college.<br /> <br /> Some players can also take the concept a little far and see Touchstones as opportunities to engage in a little Count Dracula-esque stalking. Depending on the game group, the controlling and abusive nature of a vampire might be something a group is interested in exploring while others may run the hell away since they just wanted to wear trench coats while swinging katanas ala <i>Blade</i>. Here are some tips for running Touchstones in V5.<br /> <br /> <b>1. Let the player provide the concept</b><br /> <br /> A Storyteller should primarily consider a Touchstone an in-character resource for their players rather than a tool for themselves. It is a part of the player character's background and something that they should define as well as be able to define as they see fit. It can be as close or as distant as the player wishes to make the relationship. Storytellers shouldn't attempt to encourage players to fit in any particular mold of what sort of Touchstone they want to define and be flexible about what they allow even if some concepts don't fit the mold.<br /> <br /> A player character may have a very intimate and direct relationship with their Touchstone like being their wife or parent. The player character may also have a very distant or even ridiculous one like being a huge fan of Brittney Spears or the President. They will never interact with them but their feelings regarding them might impact their character behind the scenes. There's also splitting the middle like the fact they pay for the upkeep of the orphaned child of a victim they overfed on. Your player is probably providing a clue to you how much they want to interact with the Touchstone system when they say what sort of one they want. Don't try and force the issue but go with what feels good for them.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Set the boundaries for what is acceptable</b><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><b><a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEia6yI7-wfuWbN2zGmpt4vliWORlFODB-a4w3gMYYGhpTs1kdkaqMl_dssdGzSzNVgqVBjeE56s_Gu4K9XFOWXBTnCmLmyiXzPrnbIWWBsfSogHXBeMxxt8M5MNSnSXRxcj2t9BdSxyGK80m64o6uUZpyAaS6UliZ6gJxJ7XXDty61KEiECFLKdYKSkW8c9/s230/Untitled.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img width=\"219\" height=\"230\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEia6yI7-wfuWbN2zGmpt4vliWORlFODB-a4w3gMYYGhpTs1kdkaqMl_dssdGzSzNVgqVBjeE56s_Gu4K9XFOWXBTnCmLmyiXzPrnbIWWBsfSogHXBeMxxt8M5MNSnSXRxcj2t9BdSxyGK80m64o6uUZpyAaS6UliZ6gJxJ7XXDty61KEiECFLKdYKSkW8c9/s1600/Untitled.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEia6yI7-wfuWbN2zGmpt4vliWORlFODB-a4w3gMYYGhpTs1kdkaqMl_dssdGzSzNVgqVBjeE56s_Gu4K9XFOWXBTnCmLmyiXzPrnbIWWBsfSogHXBeMxxt8M5MNSnSXRxcj2t9BdSxyGK80m64o6uUZpyAaS6UliZ6gJxJ7XXDty61KEiECFLKdYKSkW8c9/s1600/Untitled.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEia6yI7-wfuWbN2zGmpt4vliWORlFODB-a4w3gMYYGhpTs1kdkaqMl_dssdGzSzNVgqVBjeE56s_Gu4K9XFOWXBTnCmLmyiXzPrnbIWWBsfSogHXBeMxxt8M5MNSnSXRxcj2t9BdSxyGK80m64o6uUZpyAaS6UliZ6gJxJ7XXDty61KEiECFLKdYKSkW8c9/s1600/Untitled.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a></b></div> <br /> Players may well want to engage with the Touchstone system in a very direct and overt way by making their Touchstone a part of the game. They may want their Touchstone to be their ghoul or consort that has a daily role in their vampiric unlife. <i>Vampire: The Masquerade: Bloodlines</i> had the character of Heather that the Fledgling exerted complete control over, taking over their life after Heather drank their blood once.<br /> <br /> Without going too far, the game dealt with some deeply uncomfortable topics like Heather's blood addiction results in her abandoning her family as well as college before potentially losing her mind to kidnap victims for her master. Indeed, if the player character does not dismiss Heather, she will eventually meet her death at the hands of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> However, when I say that it didn't go too far, I should note that it didn't go too far for me. Quite a few players were absolutely appalled by the storyline and dismissed Heather immediately. Which is fine, it depends on the player and their characters. Know what your players are comfortable and want from their Touchstones.<br /> <br /> <b>3. Don't use them purely as a weakness</b><br /> <br /> The only rules provided for Touchstones is for them to be a tool Storytellers to screw with player characters. Basically, if something happens to a Touchstone or they change in a way that disappoints a vampire's exaggerated sense of their goodness then they may take Stains. This is a bad way to run them in my mind and I feel that Touchstones should be viewed as a net good by Kindred. This doesn't need to be mechanical but a strong link between Humanity, Convictions, and Chronicle Tenets should be established. It would not be remiss for a Storyteller to award an extra point of Experience for players incorporating their Touchstones in-game or giving Willpower rewards or removing Stains related to them.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Use them effectively but sparingly</b><br /> <br /> Touchstones are individualized for each player character, so time spent with them is almost inherently not time the group would be experiencing together. You can get around this if they're one of the player's ghouls or have a role like a bartender at the Succubus Club but, in general, they're not going to interact much with the group as a whole. This is a good thing as they shouldn't dominate a chronicle but be used for short scenes or be background elements. Touchstones are best used in moderation and for when the player wishes to act with them as a prop. Visiting a player character's now-senile son in a nursing home is the Storyteller giving said player character's player the chance to show off their drama chops but is going to be a spotlight for one player character, not the entire coterie.<br /> <br /> <b>5. Allow the player to dictate their relationship</b><br /> <br /> A quick and dirty trick I learned is that players hate when the Storyteller does horrible things to their characters but absolutely love it when they do horrible things to their characters. Maybe my players are just sadists but they love setting up nightmarish scenarios where they describe the terrible backstories or torments I give them in-game permission to come up with. As such, it's entirely okay to ask the players if they have an endgame for how they see their player character's relationship with their Touchstone ending.<br /> <br /> You can go differently but in general, having a pre-agreed upon idea is not bad for it even if it's, &quot;I see Dave the Brujah's relationship with Stephanie ending in disaster.&quot; It could also be, &quot;Eventually Dave the Brujah's enemies will probably get her or he'll reveal the Masquerade to her.&quot; But could more often be the PC wanting to devise something particularly twisted they'll play out on their own with the coteries help. I bring this up because one of my players wrote out a frenzy scene where his character drank from his sister after killing their parents and traumatized her into insanity, causing him to seek a way to erase her memory. It was profoundly twisted. All on his player too.<br /> <br /> <b>6. If romantic, allow the players to play out the scenes themselves</b><br /> <br /> Touchstones can indeed be romantic in nature but this is another area where the inclinations of the table need to be taken into account. If making a romantic interest, the player should be the ones to create them. Storytellers can suggest they prefer to go with, &quot;Goth Girl&quot;, &quot;Hippie Chick&quot;, &quot;Handsome Doctor&quot; over &quot;International Super Star&quot; or &quot;Billionaire Tech Mogul&quot; unless they buy the proper backgrounds. Still, if they want to progress it romantically, the best solution I suggest is to allow players to write out or play out their own scenes when dealing with the issue. It helps resolve any awkwardness there. As stated, players love melodrama and surrendering some control is a good decision there.<br /> <br /> <b>7. Don't be afraid to offer the option to &quot;upgrade&quot; your Touchstone</b><br /> <br /> One of the elements inherent to being a vampire is the act of siring. This is something that player characters rarely do in-game unless they're making cannon fodder like the Sabbat. They often have very light and unimportant relationships with their childer. As such, offering player characters the chance in-universe to Embrace by their Prince or Baron should be a thing they might consider for a Touchstone. This will allow them to be an NPC of greater importance to the game.<br /> <br /> According to the rules this will cause Stains and willpower loss but as an ST you might be willing to wave that or at least ask the player to go through that for that for the sake of the roleplaying opportunity. Their Touchstone will now have a much more important role in the game and more akin to a sidekick or henchman. This can also apply to ghouldom but that comes with its own roleplaying challenges.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh9IOXTJQWN0qU6h4qS6KnUK9QNwzBWc8p6_7WRi5mRI8mk30WtnGybQ3eGwNyTMuSOlUORSm9JC1WAzPKFEp2egj7E3Oly28fJ3r7os74Jp7XWH-qh_jsp-VxuwlJ9OwtbBxODEmHaJC5OE1OKV50rcOMDpR3Ic7FcT46Gz4RaDPWttK1XXG9aNGT8z0OO/s500/Dracula-gary-oldman-79336_500_264.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><img width=\"320\" height=\"169\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh9IOXTJQWN0qU6h4qS6KnUK9QNwzBWc8p6_7WRi5mRI8mk30WtnGybQ3eGwNyTMuSOlUORSm9JC1WAzPKFEp2egj7E3Oly28fJ3r7os74Jp7XWH-qh_jsp-VxuwlJ9OwtbBxODEmHaJC5OE1OKV50rcOMDpR3Ic7FcT46Gz4RaDPWttK1XXG9aNGT8z0OO/s320/Dracula-gary-oldman-79336_500_264.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh9IOXTJQWN0qU6h4qS6KnUK9QNwzBWc8p6_7WRi5mRI8mk30WtnGybQ3eGwNyTMuSOlUORSm9JC1WAzPKFEp2egj7E3Oly28fJ3r7os74Jp7XWH-qh_jsp-VxuwlJ9OwtbBxODEmHaJC5OE1OKV50rcOMDpR3Ic7FcT46Gz4RaDPWttK1XXG9aNGT8z0OO/s320/Dracula-gary-oldman-79336_500_264.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEh9IOXTJQWN0qU6h4qS6KnUK9QNwzBWc8p6_7WRi5mRI8mk30WtnGybQ3eGwNyTMuSOlUORSm9JC1WAzPKFEp2egj7E3Oly28fJ3r7os74Jp7XWH-qh_jsp-VxuwlJ9OwtbBxODEmHaJC5OE1OKV50rcOMDpR3Ic7FcT46Gz4RaDPWttK1XXG9aNGT8z0OO/s320/Dracula-gary-oldman-79336_500_264.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></a><br /> <br /> <b>8. Don't be afraid to &quot;award&quot; Touchstones in-game</b><br /> <br /> Players are annoyed by the prospect of losing their Touchstones because they first are being asked to care about an NPC followed by the fact that it will be a pain if they do suffer any damage to them. This should be mitigated by the prospect of being able to acquire them in-game. Storytellers should tell a player when they have the opportunity to acquire a new Touchstone as well as whatever benefits they might want to get from devoting time to the relationship. Making them Allies or Contacts can also encourage them not to resent the vulnerability that an extra Touchstone represents.<br /> <br /> <b>9. Remember NPC Kindred have Touchstones too</b><br /> <br /> While a new rule, the lore has long established that Kindred have a dangerous fascination with mortals. Long before Vampire: The Masquerade, the undead would stalk and obsess over specific individuals far beyond their value as a next meal. Indeed, Carmilla stalked Laura since probable childhood. Which is to say nothing says that the player characters can't find out about other vampire's &quot;weaknesses&quot; and using them may be better than the player's own. What if Dave the Brujah's girlfriend has been kidnapped by Hunters? They force him to become an informant. Do they help rescue her or destroy him for betraying them? What if they learn about the Prince's mistress and receive offers for her identity from the Prince's enemies or her family that want to &quot;rescue&quot; her from his attentions?<br /> <br /> <b>10. Touchstones should be, above all else, interesting</b><br /> <br /> At the end of the day, Touchstones are just another tool in the Storyteller arsenal. They're meant to encourage the ST and player both to think about how to include more mortals in a vampire's life as things other than food. If they're not entertaining then they shouldn't show up. Use Touchstones as much as your story will benefit from them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T11:52:46-08:00","id":1527127,"title":"","content":"Very good tips there and I mentioned on another post that my Malkavian to his surprise is having romantic feelings towards his main touchstone and is conflicted about it as she is a direct descendant of his childhood best friend from London England and she to him is practically family and tries to keep her safe from his world and doesn't want to ghoul or embrace her as he is aware enough that nothing good happens in the long run. It's makes for a good personal story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T21:57:31-08:00","id":1527139,"title":"","content":"That is a very interesting topic. How it applies to path vampires? Being humane and all sounds pretty interesting as a concept, but how do I do to explore the socially inacceptable, like carving magnificent twirls in a live human to see how their body survives, or to make an artistic statement? And would there be a touchstone that's ok with that? Is there a way to Sabbath vampires to drop them entirely without going wassail on the drop of a hat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-20T22:26:22-08:00","id":1527140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527121-ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5?p=1527139#post1527139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is a very interesting topic. How it applies to path vampires? Being humane and all sounds pretty interesting as a concept, but how do I do to explore the socially inacceptable, like carving magnificent twirls in a live human to see how their body survives, or to make an artistic statement? And would there be a touchstone that's ok with that? Is there a way to Sabbath vampires to drop them entirely without going wassail on the drop of a hat?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to draw a in-universe justification, having a Touchstone may be the reason that V5 vampires have Stains rather than automatic losses while Sabbat and non-Touchstone vampires use the old rules. Thus showing a direct reason why vampires might cultivate Touchstones as a definite way of lessening the dangers of humanity loss. Though in the Sabbat's case, they have Paths of Enlightenment and thus don't need Touchstones.<br /> <br /> But of course with Chronicle Tenets, you could literally have Humanity loss and Touchstones built around torturing specific mortals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T09:57:27-08:00","id":1527170,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm trying to hit a balance between experimenting with how low a mortal can go and still be human, by default. I mean, Charles Manson did things that were inhuman, but no matter how debased and awful Charles Manson and the Manson Family and Aleister Crowley and his Astra Argentum, they were human. So, by being born human and not having a Beast you are human, but by the circumstances of being embraced now I must be a nice little undead chasing after whatever justification to keep as a rational bring and not dropping on wassail. I frankly like to search the limits of humanity and inhumanity, and if a human will ever not be a human anymore, and if a vampire will fall in a bad night or not. You see, kinda Mortal Joke. Studying how much a vampire and a mortal can debased themselves while still being human, you see? Will you feed in the heart blood of dear old mommy if the Hunger hits you and go wassail or not if you still can hold in something important. But what if your dear old touchstone brings their dear old mommy to assuage your Hunger, are they still human? And why should they still be human while you go down? What are the limits? I frankly can see a Tzimisce or Lasombra researching that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T12:04:46-08:00","id":1527180,"title":"","content":"I find the best way to use touchstones is to keep their faces prominent and their brains intact, so they are fully aware that they are part of a vozhd. This maximizes the horror Cammies feel when they look at the vozhd and see the crying faces of their loved ones.<br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.postimg.cc/28C0sRrP/Touchy.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/28C0sRrP/Touchy.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.postimg.cc/28C0sRrP/Touchy.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T12:41:29-08:00","id":1527185,"title":"","content":"Troubling but something that a Fiend would do. <br /> <br /> &quot;For you it was a horror, for me it's a Monday evening for me.&quot; quoted by a Tzismce elder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T12:52:48-08:00","id":1527187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527121-ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5?p=1527185#post1527185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Troubling but something that a Fiend would do.<br /> <br /> &quot;For you it was a horror, for me it's a Monday evening for me.&quot; quoted by a Tzismce elder.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is actually whether a Vozhd or other flesh-crafted ghoul counts as a Touchstone for a Tzimisce or whether they're all on the Paths so it doesn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T14:44:28-08:00","id":1527198,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1527187]<br /> <br /> The question is actually whether a Vozhd or other flesh-crafted ghoul counts as a Touchstone for a Tzimisce or whether they're all on the Paths so it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Maybe they might have favorite test subjects that they have grown attached to and find themselves mildly concerned about there welfare. Makes for a strange co dependent relationship like Dracula &amp; Renfeld in the recent Nicolas Cage movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T15:57:45-08:00","id":1527200,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Lysander;n1527198]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527121-ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5?p=1527187#post1527187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question is actually whether a Vozhd or other flesh-crafted ghoul counts as a Touchstone for a Tzimisce or whether they're all on the Paths so it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> Maybe they might have favorite test subjects that they have grown attached to and find themselves mildly concerned about there welfare. Makes for a strange co dependent relationship like Dracula &amp; Renfeld in the recent Nicolas Cage movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, ghouls can absolutely be Touchstones and you don't have to like your Touchstone. They're basically triggers for human emotions. Things other than blood, violence, or power.<br /> <br /> IMHO, that includes people you loathe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-21T17:18:25-08:00","id":1527210,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest Touchstones shouldn't be a net good per se, but rather somewhere between a necessary evil and &quot;the least worst option&quot; where the alternative is degeneration. They should absolutely be integral to a PC and their personal narrative, and used in ways that suit the chronicle, the themes that player wishes to explore, and the connection that Touchstone has to the player and their Conviction.<br /> <br /> The one thing I'd urge is never to <i>just </i>damsel Touchstones. Subvert the fuck out of that expectation, and if you're going to attack a PC's Touchstone, do it in ways that directly challenge the Conviction rather than just the Touchstone's life, health, or safety. It's more interesting to put the PC's <i>link</i> to the Touchstone in peril, than it is to put the Touchstone <i>themselves</i> in peril; that forces positive action on the player's part to protect the connection, and as the corebook goes out of its way to detail, that rarely works in the PC's favor as in the process of protecting their Touchstone, they usually damage or destroy it as collateral. Then the player has to deal with the moral quandry of losing the Conviction, and the potential ramifications of that choice.<br /> <br /> For instance, in this v5 chronicle I'm prepping, one of the PC's Touchstones is their mortal granddaughter, connected to a conviction about protecting the innocent. One of the chronicle tenets is to always seek and never deny truth, which already has some built-in conflict with this PC's conviction (by way of fostering untruth to protect the innocent). But I did the math on this character's age, and realized this granddaughter would have to be no younger than late teens, which means approaching college age.<br /> <br /> That's already free real estate for exploring &quot;loss of innocence&quot; themes, and not all necessarily in reductive and trope-y ways. But then I realized, in the work I've already done...lo and behold, there's a Tremere who havens at the local major university, who happens to be in House Carna and is a popular adjunct WGS studies professor.<br /> <br /> So what happens when or if this PC's Touchstone stumbles into this Tremere's class for dual or early credit, and this particular Tremere starts encouraging the Touchstone to spread her wings? Not necessarily in the creepy House Carna quasi-sexual cultish way, but in the broader &quot;coming of age&quot; way -- that directly threatens the PC's <i>connection</i> to the Touchstone without necessarily threatening the Touchstone herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-24T02:39:52-08:00","id":1527356,"title":"","content":"I tend to lean towards touchstones being an asset with risks I also tend to allow non human touchstones as long as they're a destructible concept.<br /> <br /> Ive integrated touchstones into v20 as a background. You get an xp reduction on humanity. Funny story a player wanted to have Manchester United as a touchstones, the condition was that you got +1 to frenzy if they wernt doing well irl lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 12-24-2023, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T12:20:17-08:00","id":1527571,"title":"","content":"Dam Ragged Robin having a sports team as a Touchstone is brilliant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T09:55:18-08:00","id":1527601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1527121-ten-tips-to-using-touchstones-in-v5?p=1527571#post1527571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dam Ragged Robin having a sports team as a Touchstone is brilliant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of it being something with emotional resonance rather simply and arbitrary list of pet humans. Some touchstones I've snowballed or seen so far<br /> <br /> 1) a series of portraits of a ventrue's human family.<br /> <br /> 2) a church<br /> <br /> 3) a small community in the alps<br /> <br /> 4) a wedding ring<br /> <br /> 5) a code of honor<br /> <br /> 6) a pet<br /> <br /> 7) a library of arcane grimoires<br /> <br /> The important thing is they have to be logical and destructible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T13:07:44-08:00","id":1527607,"title":"","content":"I can see that Ragged Robin. I remember that Polina's most cherished item is an antique silver cross that his very late mother gave him and that could work as a touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}